+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`src/cache.ts` keeps a module-level `Map<string, CacheEntry>` keyed by widget id (`src/cache.ts:10`). `render(widget)` (`src/cache.ts:30`) returns `get(widget.id)` when present (`src/cache.ts:12`), else renders through `renderWidget` (`src/render.ts:3`) and stores `{ html, storedAt }`. Nothing evicts, and props are never consulted. The repository has no dependencies, no lockfile and no tests (`package.json` holds only `name`, `private`, `type`). Node 26 and Bun 1.4 are installed; Bun runs the TypeScript sources directly, including the extensionless relative imports in `src/`. Motivation: proposal.md - Why. Requirements: `specs/widget-render-cache/spec.md`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Bound memory held for cached HTML, evicting in LRU order.
+- Never serve HTML rendered from props that differ from the widget's current props.
+- Keep the module's exported function signatures.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- A runtime-configurable budget, TTL expiry or per-widget budgets.
+- Counting the props snapshots against the byte budget (see Risks).
+- Making `get(id)` props-aware: it stays a lookup by id that returns the cached HTML for that id, which `render` keeps fresh. Changing its signature would break the dashboard shell outside this repository.
+
+## Decisions
+
+**D1. One entry per widget id, carrying a props snapshot.** The entry becomes `{ html, storedAt, props }`, where `props` is `structuredClone(widget.props)` taken when the HTML is rendered. `render` serves a hit only when `isDeepStrictEqual(entry.props, widget.props)`; otherwise it re-renders and overwrites the entry for that id. Alternatives: keying by id plus a props fingerprint (`JSON.stringify`) - rejected: it drops functions, `undefined` and `Map`/`Set` contents, so different props can share a fingerprint and serve stale HTML, and it leaves several entries per id, which breaks `invalidate(id)`; comparing the props reference - rejected: in-place mutation keeps the reference and serves stale HTML. The snapshot is a deep copy, so in-place mutation is detected. Class instances lose their prototype in the clone and never compare equal, so such widgets always re-render: a safe miss, never a stale hit.
+
+**D2. Unclonable props bypass the cache.** When `structuredClone` throws (`DataCloneError`, for example a function value), `render` deletes any entry for the id, renders, and returns without storing. Alternative: cache by id ignoring props - rejected, it is the stale-HTML defect this change removes.
+
+**D3. Storage and eviction through `lru-cache`.** The `Map` is replaced by `new LRUCache<string, CacheEntry>({ maxSize: MAX_CACHE_BYTES, sizeCalculation: (e) => Math.max(1, Buffer.byteLength(e.html, "utf8")) })`. `maxEntrySize` defaults to `maxSize`, so `set` of an oversized entry stores nothing and deletes the existing entry for that key (`lru-cache` `src/index.ts` `set`, the `maxEntrySize` branch), which is exactly the oversized requirement. `get` updates recency and `has` does not by default, matching the LRU requirement. `Math.max(1, ...)` keeps the size a positive integer, which `lru-cache` requires; `renderWidget` output is never empty in practice. `invalidate` maps to `delete`, `clear` to `clear`, `size()` to the `size` property (entry count). `MAX_CACHE_BYTES = 1_048_576` is an exported `const`.
+
+**D4. Tests with `bun test`.** `test/cache.test.ts` drives the module through its exports with stub widgets whose `render()` counts calls and returns sized strings; `clear()` runs in `beforeEach` because the cache is a module singleton. `package.json` gains `"test": "bun test"`. Bun is the runner because it executes the existing extensionless TypeScript imports without a build step or `tsconfig`.
+
+### Build vs. adopt: size-bounded LRU cache
+- Repository: none; searched `src/cache.ts`, `src/render.ts`, `src/widget.ts`, `package.json` (no dependencies, no `node_modules`).
+- Platform: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map (insertion-ordered `Map`, the primitive an LRU is built from; no size accounting or eviction) and https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html#static-method-bufferbytelengthstring-encoding (UTF-8 byte length); neither provides eviction by size.
+- Candidates: `lru-cache` https://github.com/isaacs/node-lru-cache; newest release 11.5.3, 2026-09-18; BlueOak-1.0.0; maintained; adopt (`maxSize` + `sizeCalculation` + `maxEntrySize` cover the byte budget, LRU order and oversized rejection). `quick-lru` https://github.com/sindresorhus/quick-lru; newest release 7.3.0, 2025-10-10; MIT; maintained; reject, gap: `maxSize` counts items, not bytes, and its dual-cache design holds up to 2 × `maxSize` items, breaking a strict bound. `mnemonist` https://github.com/yomguithereal/mnemonist; newest release 0.40.7, 2026-11-03; MIT; maintained; reject, gap: its `LRUCache` capacity counts entries, with no per-entry size.
+- Decision: adopt `lru-cache` ^11.5.3.
+
+### Build vs. adopt: props snapshot and deep equality
+- Repository: none; searched the same paths.
+- Platform: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/structuredClone (deep copy, handles `Map`, `Set`, `Date`, cycles; throws `DataCloneError` on functions) and https://nodejs.org/api/util.html#utilisdeepstrictequalval1-val2 (deep strict equality, prototype-aware); both available in Node 26 and Bun 1.4 (checked with a scratch script outside the repository).
+- Candidates: not searched, covered above.
+- Decision: adopt `structuredClone` and `node:util` `isDeepStrictEqual`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Props snapshots are not counted in the budget, so real memory exceeds 1 MiB by the size of the cloned props] → props are small configuration objects next to rendered HTML; the budget is documented as an HTML-byte bound in the spec.
+- [Deep clone and compare on every render add CPU per widget] → the dashboard renders about 40 widgets per refresh and props are small; still far below a re-render.
+- [Widgets whose props hold functions or class instances are never cached] → correct over fast; the shell can move such values out of props if it matters.
+- [1 MiB may be too small or large for real boards] → a single exported constant; change it in one place.
+- [New runtime dependency] → one package, no transitive runtime dependencies in 11.x, pinned by the lockfile.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+No data migration: the cache is in-process and empty at start. Rollback is reverting the commit; the exported API is unchanged.
