+# Gate
+
+- **Mandatory class**: none
+- **Depth**: standard (the class is none and no review, gate or release mechanism changes)
+- **Risk tier**: product
+- **Author's risk assessment**: The change rewrites the dashboard's in-process render cache. A wrong freshness check either serves HTML from outdated props (users see wrong widget content until the next invalidate) or misses on every call (the cache stops saving render time); a wrong size calculation lets the cache exceed its 1 MiB HTML budget or evict too eagerly. Nothing is persisted, no data leaves the process and the cache starts empty on every load, so every failure ends at a reload or revert. The cache's operations are synchronous in single-threaded JavaScript, with no interleaving between check and store, so it is not `concurrency-state`; exported signatures stay the same and no independently released consumer exists, so it is not `wire-contract-api`. `product` because it ships in the dashboard users see.
+- **Whole-diff review**: not needed (whole-diff surface reviewed in F2)
+- **Accepted residual risks**: Props snapshots held in cache entries are not counted against the 1 MiB budget, so process memory for the cache exceeds the HTML bound by the size of the cloned props (design.md - Risks); widgets whose props hold functions or class instances are never served from the cache.
+- **Out of scope for blocking**: Choice of the 1 MiB default and making it configurable (a tuning follow-up); `get(id)` staying a props-unaware lookup by id (design.md - Non-Goals).
