+# Tasks
+
+Every test named below is written before its implementation and seen failing against the current `src/cache.ts` (or failing to load where the export it needs does not exist yet). Each task's tests sit in one `describe` block named by the `-t` pattern its Verify uses (`byte budget`, `LRU order`, `oversized`, `invalidation`, `props freshness`, `unclonable props`); `bun test -t` matches that pattern against `describe` + test names, so a task's Verify runs exactly its tests.
+
+## 1. Setup
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add the runtime dependency `lru-cache@^11.5.3` with `bun add`, committing `bun.lock`, and add `"test": "bun test"` to `package.json` scripts (design.md D3, D4). Verify: `bun install --frozen-lockfile && bun -e "const { LRUCache } = await import('lru-cache'); if (typeof LRUCache !== 'function') process.exit(1)" && bun -e "if (require('./package.json').scripts?.test !== 'bun test') process.exit(1)"`
+
+## 2. Byte-bounded LRU storage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Replace the module `Map` in `src/cache.ts` with an `LRUCache` of `CacheEntry` keyed by widget id, bounded by the exported `const MAX_CACHE_BYTES = 1_048_576` and sized by `Math.max(1, Buffer.byteLength(entry.html, "utf8"))` (design.md D3); map `get`, `has`, `invalidate`, `clear` and `size()` onto it with unchanged signatures, and update the module's header comment to state the byte budget and LRU eviction. Add `test/cache.test.ts` with stub widgets that count `render()` calls and return sized strings, `clear()` in `beforeEach`, and the tests for requirement "Cached HTML stays within the byte budget": three 400,000-byte widgets leave two entries; two widgets of 300,000 `€` leave only the second; `MAX_CACHE_BYTES` reads 1,048,576. Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "byte budget"`
+- [ ] 2.2 Add the tests for requirement "Least recently used entries are evicted first": a render hit on `a` before rendering `c` evicts `b`; a `get("a")` before rendering `c` evicts `b`; a `has("a")` before rendering `c` evicts `a`. Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "LRU order"`
+- [ ] 2.3 Add the tests for requirement "HTML larger than the budget is not cached": a 1,100,000-byte re-render of cached `a` returns that HTML, leaves no entry for `a` and keeps `s`; a widget whose complete HTML (wrapper included) is exactly 1,048,576 bytes is cached as the only entry and one of 1,048,577 bytes is not. Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "oversized"`
+- [ ] 2.4 Add the tests for requirement "Explicit invalidation and entry count": after caching `a` and `b`, `invalidate("a")` leaves `size()` at 1 and the next render of `a` calls its `render()`; `clear()` leaves `size()` at 0. Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "invalidation"`
+
+## 3. Props freshness
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Store `structuredClone(widget.props)` in each `CacheEntry` and make `render` serve a hit only when `isDeepStrictEqual(entry.props, widget.props)` (from `node:util`), otherwise re-render and replace the entry for that id (design.md D1); extend the header comment with the props rule. Add the tests for requirements "Cached HTML is served for unchanged props" (a new but equal props object is a hit, one `render()` call) and "Changed props re-render and replace the entry" (`{ n: 1 }` then `{ n: 2 }` returns the new HTML with `size()` 1; a nested value mutated in place on the same props object returns HTML from the mutated props). Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "props freshness"`
+- [ ] 3.2 When `structuredClone` throws, delete any entry for the id, render and return without storing (design.md D2). Add the tests for requirement "Props without a snapshot bypass the cache": `{ onClick: () => {} }` rendered twice calls `render()` twice and `has("f")` is false, including when `f` was cached with clonable props before. Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "unclonable props"`
+
+## 4. Final verification
+
+- [ ] 4.1 Full suite after the last code commit, so the groups' tests pass together on one module instance. Verify: `bun test`
+- [ ] 4.2 F1. Manual QA on the real surface: merge the default branch (`main`) into the work branch when it is not an ancestor of the head, and commit; then, on the head after the last code commit, drive the exported `src/cache.ts` API with real `renderWidget` output from a throwaway `bun` script outside the repository and capture its printed observations (`size()`, `has`, render-call counts, returned HTML byte lengths) per row, at `standard` depth (one row per requirement plus the three minimum rows), each to its evidence path under `.omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache-size-eviction/f1/`: `r1.md` unchanged props, the second render of an equal props object makes no `render()` call; `r2.md` changed props, `{ n: 2 }` and an in-place nested mutation each return the new HTML and `size()` stays 1; `r3.md` unclonable props, two renders make two `render()` calls and `has` is false; `r4.md` byte budget, with 400,000-byte and `€` widgets the summed `Buffer.byteLength` of cached HTML is never above 1,048,576; `r5.md` LRU order, a render hit and `get` protect `a` and `has` does not; `r6.md` oversized, 1,100,000-byte HTML is returned, not cached, and the other entry is kept; `r7.md` invalidation, sizes read 1 then 0 and `a` renders fresh after `invalidate`; `m1.md` happy path, 40 widgets rendered twice, the second pass makes 0 `render()` calls and returns identical HTML; `m2.md` riskiest edge, complete HTML of exactly 1,048,576 bytes is cached and 1,048,577 bytes is not; `m3.md` adjacent regression, the returned and `get(id)` HTML equal `renderWidget(widget)` byte for byte and `has(id)` is true after a store. Verify: `bash -c 'for r in r1 r2 r3 r4 r5 r6 r7 m1 m2 m3; do test -s .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache-size-eviction/f1/$r.md || { echo "missing $r"; exit 1; }; done'`
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- F2 merge gate (`review-work`), after 4.2 and never a checkbox: the record binds every file of this folder by `plan_sha256`, tasks.md included, so the folder is final before the F2 snapshot.
+- Merge only after the F2 record validates.
+- Archive the change after the merge gate; archiving removes the taken follow-up from `docs/roadmap/w.md`.
